 i use  it mostly to create thumbnails and other  assets i might need for my videos and  content creation  so for instance i made all of my merch  on this as well as  all of my overlays for twitch and then  also assets for code with friends  it's pretty intuitive to use it's pretty  easy to collaborate with other people on  it  again i really appreciate it that it's  its own mac app because  i don't like using these heavy tools on  web because again it'll get lost in my  tabs or it's just not as efficient  and so being able to use it as a mac app  regardless of how it's built underneath  has been  a really good thing for my workflow all  right so next we'll talk about my coding  tool  so i'm an ios developer so literally  like the main  ide that i would use is xcode i have it  on my dock at the bottom  and if you're going to make ios apps you  have to use xcode  i don't really got a choice and so  yeah it's there right now i'm on 12.0.1  and yeah it's easy to access it's it's  how you  write apple apps and for everything  that's not ios development then i use  visual studio code  i've been through all the iterations of  going from sublime to  atom and it seems like now visual studio  code is like the de facto code editor  and i like it a lot i like that i can  add extensions to it the organization of  everything is really easy  being able to preview markup files has  been a real life saver as well  i'm not really a heavy user of visual  studio code because i'm not a web  developer but i know that a lot of web  developers like using this and it's a  really powerful product if you want to  use it that way  next on the dock we've got spotify  usually when i'm listening to music i'm  usually on spotify because that's where  all of my music is  spotify now next is notes so in the  video where i talk about how i organize  my life i talk about the various  note-taking systems that i have  and then notes app i use it as just kind  of like a note-taking dump  i use it as like a scratch pad really to  like copy paste  instagram captions as well as just like  quick to-do lists as well  and so just having a place that i can go  to to just like write something out  really fast right on my doc is why notes  is one of my most used apps on mac  honestly i should probably go and like  clear a lot of things out because  there's just a lot of  random notes in here that make zero  sense  so that's notes next i've got my slew of  communication tools  so i have messages on here so i can like  talk to my friends during the workday  i've also got discord because i have my  own server for people who watch my  twitch stream  and then i've got slack because i just  belong to i feel like so many different  and random slack groups and keep in  touch with folks every once in a while i  also have zoom down here because  our life is like on zoom nowadays since  we're in quarantine  and i use it at least once a day and  then i also have whatsapp mostly to  communicate with my brand manager  as well as people who live overseas and  lastly i've got lastpass which is my  password manager  just having it there so i can either  generate a new password or copy paste an  existing one  has made it super easy i also have the  chrome extension for lastpass as well  but that also deserves a spot on my dock  we're gonna skip over quicktime player  it's usually not in my dock but it's  there just because i'm recording my  screen right now  but next are the folders that i have and  in that i've got downloads  a lot of the stuff that i draw on my  ipad i airdropped my computer which then  lands and downloads and having this fan  out  view has been really easy to work with  because then i can just grab  things that have been downloaded to my  computer or airdropped i've also got my  dropbox folder because i put a lot of my  business things in there  and then i also have my videos folder  this just makes it super easy for when  i'm video editing and i need like a  quick asset